      "side": 1,
      "message": "Being more explicit seems preferable to me, so I like the idea of splitting up the calls that way in the future.\n\n`fType` and `fPrioritizeGpuReads` are not currently used beyond just passing them into the `Buffer` constructor to sit there as member attributes, so they can safely be removed unless we have intentions for them... Demonstrative CL: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/616820\n\nDid you mean to say that if anything does, in fact, use those attributes then we could land this as-is? I imagine if `fBufferType` and `fPrioritizeGpuReads` are unsued/deleted, then that would justify landing this in this way, not the other way around. Let me know if I misunderstood.",
